<title>USA: Young Broadcasting sells $200 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Young Broadcasting sells $200 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Young Broadcasting Inc was priced in the 144A private placement on Tuesday via sole manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc., according to a syndicate source.</p>
<p>BORROWER YOUNG BROADCASTING INC</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 8.75 PCT   MATURITY 6/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 99.08   FIRST PAY DATE 12/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B2    YIELD 8.89 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>S&amp;P SINGLE-B	 SPREAD 250 BP     CALLABLE  NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678</p>
